@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+Fixed `ConsolidatedMetadata` dropping child nodes when reconstructing the nested
+node tree from the flat, persisted metadata mapping. Children whose keys were not
+adjacent in the mapping (most visibly, siblings whose names differ only by case)
+were left as slash-containing keys at the top level instead of being nested under
+their parent group. The reconstructed hierarchy no longer depends on the order of
+the keys in the flat mapping.
